WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.085 --> 00:00:08.995
"Wow," Ally thought. "Ray is nervous about this gala."

2
00:00:08.996 --> 00:00:14.186
"The League of Rocket Scientists read about the diner in Gourmet Greta's column," Ray said.

3
00:00:14.187 --> 00:00:18.017
"They love our space theme, but they want a special menu for their dinner.

4
00:00:18.018 --> 00:00:24.586
I was thinking of serving grilled salmon, but what would I call it?"

5
00:00:24.587 --> 00:00:29.587
"I bet Ally can think of some out-of-this-world ideas," Mateo said.

6
00:00:29.588 --> 00:00:32.928
"Solar Salmon!" Ally suggested.

7
00:00:32.929 --> 00:00:39.697
"Hey, Ray," Randy, the assistant cook, called from Ray's office. "You've got a phone call."

8
00:00:39.698 --> 00:00:43.449
"Coming!" Ray hurried to his office.

9
00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:48.377
"Ally, what are some of the best meals in the galaxy?" Mateo asked.

10
00:00:48.378 --> 00:00:52.041
"Hmm . . . I'd say Formarian Frittata and . . ."

11
00:00:52.042 --> 00:00:58.574
Ally trailed off when she spotted the new waiter, Barry, outside, taking pictures of the diner.

12
00:00:58.575 --> 00:01:04.282
Ally had learned a lot about humans, but Barry's behavior was still mysterious to her at times.

13
00:01:04.283 --> 00:01:06.802
"What's he taking pictures of?"

14
00:01:06.803 --> 00:01:11.287
Mateo turned to look, but as soon as Barry saw them looking, he put his phone away.

15
00:01:11.288 --> 00:01:18.835
Then he rushed inside and sat down at the counter next to Phil.

16
00:01:18.836 --> 00:01:24.409
Mateo shrugged. "Why does Barry do a lot of the things he does?"

17
00:01:24.410 --> 00:01:34.184
Ally quickly read Barry's mind, but as usual, he was thinking about ways to make his father proud.

18
00:01:34.185 --> 00:01:36.952
"Back to ideas for Ray," Ally said.

19
00:01:36.953 --> 00:01:40.676
"Formarian Frittata would make a great appetizer.

20
00:01:40.677 --> 00:01:44.035
And Meltron Moon Pies could be a fun dessert, oh, and—"

21
00:01:44.036 --> 00:01:47.983
"That was the league's secretary on the phone." Ray hurried over.

22
00:01:47.984 --> 00:01:53.178
"They want to make sure that you work at the gala, Ally. They want to see your tricks."

23
00:01:53.179 --> 00:01:57.170
"Sure!" Ally said brightly.

24
00:01:57.171 --> 00:02:03.601
But inside she was nervous. "Do these rocket scientists want to be entertained?" she thought.

25
00:02:03.602 --> 00:02:08.132
"Or have they heard rumors about me? I'd better be careful."

26
00:02:08.133 --> 00:02:13.415
"Tricks? Gala?" Barry's ears perked up.

27
00:02:13.416 --> 00:02:15.867
"Can I work too, Ray? Please?"

28
00:02:15.868 --> 00:02:19.262
Ray nodded. "I need everyone that night."

29
00:02:19.263 --> 00:02:25.088
He gathered up the cookbooks and went to the kitchen.

30
00:02:25.089 --> 00:02:29.609
Barry looked at Ally. "Now you'll have to teach me your tricks."

31
00:02:29.610 --> 00:02:37.130
Ally sighed. "Fine. We can begin tomorrow when we're both working."

32
00:02:37.131 --> 00:02:44.293
"Yes!" Barry pumped his arm in triumph and went back to sit with Phil.

33
00:02:44.294 --> 00:02:54.296
Mateo shot her a look. "You can't teach him how to levitate a plate, can you?" he whispered.

34
00:02:54.297 --> 00:02:57.037
"Of course not," Ally said.

35
00:02:57.038 --> 00:03:02.175
"But he keeps asking me to teach him tricks, and I can't keep making excuses.

36
00:03:02.176 --> 00:03:06.292
That might make him even more suspicious of me. Don't worry."

37
00:03:06.293 --> 00:03:10.773
She glanced at the bag of coils. "I have a plan."

38
00:03:10.774 --> 00:03:13.597
Mateo nodded, but he still looked worried.

39
00:03:13.598 --> 00:03:21.999
"I hope it works. I'm meeting Bethany for a bike ride in the park. See you later."

40
00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:29.220
After Ally started her shift, one of her first customers was a woman at the counter.

41
00:03:29.221 --> 00:03:32.941
She barely looked up from her phone when Ally came to take her order.

42
00:03:32.942 --> 00:03:37.921
"I'll have five gallons of silver paint, please," the woman said.

43
00:03:37.922 --> 00:03:41.905
"We only serve yellow paint here," Ally joked.

44
00:03:41.906 --> 00:03:51.139
The woman looked up and laughed. "Sorry! I'm so distracted by my work."

45
00:03:51.140 --> 00:03:54.210
"Why do you need silver paint?" Ally asked.

46
00:03:54.211 --> 00:04:02.901
"I've been commissioned by the Sandville Arts Board to create sculptures from objects found or seen around town.

47
00:04:02.902 --> 00:04:08.346
I need silver paint to finish a sculpture."

48
00:04:08.347 --> 00:04:12.914
"I've seen a few of your sculptures—they're great!" Ally said.

49
00:04:12.915 --> 00:04:15.446
"Thanks," the artist replied.

50
00:04:15.447 --> 00:04:22.306
"I still have one more piece to make. I'm looking for something with a real wow factor."

51
00:04:22.307 --> 00:04:26.213
"There are some interesting things in the park," Ally said.

52
00:04:26.214 --> 00:04:30.965
"The bandshell, the murals, even the trees are inspiring!"

53
00:04:30.966 --> 00:04:35.163
The artist smiled. "Thanks. I'm Sarah by the way.

54
00:04:35.164 --> 00:04:39.358
Oh, and I'll have the Space Cakes, please."

55
00:04:39.359 --> 00:04:43.042
"One order of pancakes coming up!"

56
00:04:43.043 --> 00:04:48.029
As Ally went to put in Sarah's order, she had another inspiration.

57
00:04:48.030 --> 00:04:56.667
"I know what Mateo should do for Bethany's surprise! I can't wait to tell him!"

58
00:04:56.668 --> 00:04:59.593
Ally headed home from her shift in a good mood.

59
00:04:59.594 --> 00:05:05.755
Even though last night's dream had made her miss home, she had a lot to be thankful for here on Earth.

60
00:05:05.756 --> 00:05:09.936
"Today I helped both Ray and Sarah solve problems.

61
00:05:09.937 --> 00:05:18.511
By the time I get back to Astralia, I'm going to have a long list of good deeds," Ally thought.

62
00:05:18.512 --> 00:05:27.345
"I'll ask Alpha to keep a log for me!"

63
00:05:27.346 --> 00:05:31.221
Ally stopped near the trees and held up her meld medallion to reveal her pod.

64
00:05:31.222 --> 00:05:33.922
But to her surprise, nothing happened.

65
00:05:33.923 --> 00:05:38.886
She held it up again, but still the pod didn't appear.

66
00:05:38.887 --> 00:05:45.892
"Oh no!" Ally gasped. Her pod had vanished!

